# Build-runner transient state. The cloud-init preview embeds Neon + R2 creds — NEVER
# commit. The *-service-id / *-server-id / *-instance-id files are throwaway box/service handles.
scripts/ingest/search/.hetzner-cloud-init.preview.sh
scripts/ingest/search/.hetzner-build-server-id
scripts/ingest/search/.vultr-cloud-init.preview.sh
scripts/ingest/search/.vultr-build-instance-id
scripts/ingest/search/.*-service-id

# fts-catchup transient state. `.fts-catchup-cache/` is a per-corpus resume aid for a chunked
# backfill; `.fts-index-debt.json` is the machine-readable index-coverage marker each run writes
# (INGEST_PLAYBOOK §20) — it is a report about the CURRENT table, regenerated on every run, so a
# committed copy would only ever be a stale claim about whether search needs a re-merge.
scripts/ingest/search/.fts-catchup-cache/
scripts/ingest/search/.fts-index-debt.json

# fts-hygiene working state — the audit manifest, the dry-run transcript and the export receipt.
# All of it describes ONE point in time on a table that keeps changing, and the copy that matters
# is on R2 next to the backup it indexes (`_search/hygiene-backup/<stamp>/manifest.json`). A
# committed copy would be a stale claim about which rows are duplicates, which is worse than none.
scripts/ingest/search/.fts-hygiene/
scripts/ingest/search/.vec-hygiene/

